{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Station yourself here upon your burnt-offering, and I will encounter thus.</b> Balaam said: Israel lean upon the merit of the sacrifices, from what the Holy One, blessed be He, promised Abraham (Genesis 15:5): ״כה יהיה זרעך״ — 'so shall your seed be,' and they lean upon the merit of the priestly blessing, in which it is written (Numbers 6:23): ״כה תברכו את בני ישראל״ — 'so shall you bless the children of Israel,' and so Moses said against the king of Edom (ibid. 20): ״כה אמר אחיך ישראל״ — 'so says your brother Israel.' Therefore, 'station yourself here upon your burnt-offering' — you take one and I will take the other, and this is what he said: 'and I will encounter thus' — you with your sacrifice and I with my wisdom. Thus did our Rabbis of blessed memory interpret."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:23.299092190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}